Name: chrome-pak-customizer
Short Name: pak
URL: https://github.com/myfreeer/chrome-pak-customizer
Version: 3.0.0
Revision: f8cd97465392291290132bf195d700aa7adb30f0
Branch: 3.x
License: MIT
License File: LICENSE

Description:
A Rust command-line tool for unpacking and repacking Chromium PAK v4 and v5
resource files, including Brotli-compressed resources and the Microsoft Edge
v5 resource-ID variant.

Local modifications:
- Thorium-specific README and source metadata.
- Cross-platform Python build, test, clean, and atomic publishing entry point.
- Retains Thorium's version command, Chromium ASCII art, colored status output,
  and pack statistics while correcting legacy command-status defects.
- Existing Thorium prebuilt filenames are retained while 3.x binaries undergo
  release validation.
- Thorium setup and installer integration remains outside the upstream source.

Upstream files intentionally not vendored:
- .github/
- script/
- README.md

The checked-in Rust source is based on the revision above with the listed
Thorium CLI changes. Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, .cargo/config.toml, and LICENSE
are synchronized without local changes.
